From: Douglas Teles <dga.teles@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: rockchip: sai: offer only the channels the lanes can play

The SAI advertises up to 512 channels; outside TDM, hw_params then
rejects anything over two per wired lane. On the RK3562 consoles (one
TX lane) WirePlumber probes 8 channels at every start and fills the log
with "not enough lanes (1) for requested number of playback channels
(8)" and ASoC -22 errors. Constrain the channels at startup instead.

---
--- a/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c	2026-11-24 13:33:42.337972388 -0300
+++ b/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c	2026-11-24 13:33:42.351886264 -0300
@@ -897,6 +897,23 @@
 	if (sai->wait_time[stream])
 		substream->wait_time = sai->wait_time[stream];
 
+	/*
+	 * Outside TDM each lane carries two channels: offer only what the
+	 * wired lanes can play, so a sound server does not probe more and
+	 * fail in hw_params ("not enough lanes").
+	 */
+	if (!sai->is_tdm) {
+		unsigned int lanes = stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK ?
+				     sai->tx_lanes : sai->rx_lanes;
+		int ret;
+
+		ret = snd_pcm_hw_constraint_minmax(substream->runtime,
+						   SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_CHANNELS,
+						   1, 2 * lanes);
+		if (ret < 0)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	sai->substreams[stream] = substream;
 
 	return 0;
